sity Press</publisher-name><fpage>377</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14634304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>McCarl</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Economic Potential of Biomass Based Fuels for Greenhouse Gas Emission Mitigation</article-title><source>Environmental &#x00026; Resource Economics</source><year>2003</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>312</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1023632309097</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sohngen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendesohn</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An Optimal Control Model of Forest Carbon Sequestration</article-title><source>American Journal of Agricultural Economics</source><year>2003</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>448</fpage><lpage>457</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/1467-8276.00133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Vellen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Land-use changes in Australia and the Kyoto protocol</article-title><source>Environmental, Science and Policy</source><year>1999</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>144</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1462-9011(99)00007-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nabuurs</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dolman</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Verkaik</surname><given-names>E</given-names